From: Liuqin Linux Kit maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: liuqin: preserve the board USB Gen1 limit

The shipping Liuqin DT limits DWC3 to SuperSpeed and forces Gen1.
Without a board ceiling, DWC_usb31 advertises its IP-level Gen2 capability
even though this board path fails during enhanced-speed negotiation.
Use the common binding so desktop and Recovery share the same limit,
including gadgets that leave their own maximum speed at its default.
The existing DWC3 core also programs LLUCTL.ForceGen1 for this DRD IP.

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8475-xiaomi-liuqin.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8475-xiaomi-liuqin.dts
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8475-xiaomi-liuqin.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8475-xiaomi-liuqin.dts
@@ -1892,6 +1892,8 @@
 	 * UDC is registered.
 	 */
 	role-switch-default-mode = "host";
+	/* The shipping board is qualified for USB 3.2 Gen1. */
+	maximum-speed = "super-speed";
 	phys = <&usb_1_hsphy>, <&usb_1_qmpphy QMP_USB43DP_USB3_PHY>;
 	phy-names = "usb2-phy", "usb3-phy";
 };
